{#-
  Full-screen search overlay, from design-source/partials/search.html.

  Site search is BUILT (features.searchEnabled). The index is compiled at build
  time by src/search-index.11ty.js into /search-index.json and queried in the
  browser by js/site-search.js — no backend, no form, no third-party service,
  and no network work beyond one same-origin fetch of that static file.

  Progressive enhancement, the same discipline as the register keyword filter
  on /receipts/: the search box ships `hidden` and only js/site-search.js
  reveals it. With JS off a reader never sees an input that does nothing — they
  see the shortcut link blocks, which is the whole of the overlay's previous
  behaviour. The "Site search is planned" note is gone with the thing it
  described; the honest fallback is the links themselves.

  The Receipts destination is now one of the same .so-links blocks rather than a
  standalone u-btn, so the overlay presents one consistent row of destinations.

  js/ui.js still owns open/close and is untouched; site-search.js takes focus
  from the `open` class ui.js sets, after ui.js's own focus() for that tick.

  DESIGN: structure fixed. CONTENT: shortcuts from _data/chrome.json.
-#}
<div class="search-ov" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="Search">
  <div class="so-top">{% image "logos/logo-tight-light.png", "", "8rem", [160, 320], "lazy", "logo-44" %}<button class="drawer-x" type="button" aria-label="Close search" data-search-close>&#10005;</button></div>
  {% if features.searchEnabled %}
  <div class="so-search" data-search-box hidden>
    <label for="site-search">Search uncost.org</label>
    <input id="site-search" type="search" placeholder="Try &ldquo;shelter&rdquo; or &ldquo;pledge&rdquo;&hellip;" autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="site-search-status">
    <p class="so-status" id="site-search-status" role="status" data-search-status></p>
    <ul class="so-results" data-search-results></ul>
  </div>
  {% endif %}
  <div class="so-links"><a href="/receipts/">Search the Receipts</a>{% for link in chrome.searchShortcuts %}<a href="{{ link.url }}">{{ link.label }}</a>{% endfor %}</div>
</div>
<script src="/js/site-search.js" defer></script>
